  "_comment": "Manifest of real .eu4 saves used by tests/test_real_saves.py. The saves themselves are NOT committed (gitignored) -- make them yourself following docs/test.md and drop them in this directory with the 'file' name below. Any entry whose file is missing is skipped, not failed. Most saves are the game's opening state for that (date, country) -- start a historical-setup game at the given bookmark, pick the country, and save immediately without unpausing or changing anything; see docs/test.md section 3. S67-S74 (19th century, no vanilla bookmark exists past 1785) are instead 'hands-off' saves -- started at the 1785 bookmark and run forward with zero player actions to the listed date; see docs/test.md section 3B. 'date' is the save's own in-game date (checked against the save, not guessed); 'tag' is the country tag the save should report as the player -- some non-major tags (S45 on) are best guesses for what's actually selectable at that bookmark, verify against your client's own bookmark country list. 'kind' is \"start\" (game-start, saved before unpausing) or \"ticked\" (a real, actively-played save with ships/transfers/AI decisions -- see docs/test.md section on ticked saves).",
